    focusWomen: true,
    bio: "Carolyn Custis James is an author who writes on women's calling and identity in Scripture, pushing back against narrow definitions of biblical womanhood that she argues sideline half the church's talent and voice. Her work is heavier on biblical and cultural argument than devotional application, often re-reading familiar Bible stories with close attention to their female characters.\n\nHer book Half the Church argues that churches under-use women's gifts relative to the scale of the biblical narrative, while Lost Women of the Bible and The Gospel of Ruth work through specific overlooked or misunderstood women in Scripture, and Women Rising extends the same argument into a fuller picture of women's flourishing in ministry.",
