    id: 'auth_n_t_wright',
    name: 'N.T. Wright',
    tagline: 'NT scholar & retired Anglican bishop',
    bio: "N.T. Wright (born 1948) is a British New Testament scholar and retired Anglican bishop who has taught at Oxford, Cambridge, and St Andrews, and is widely regarded as one of the most influential New Testament scholars of the past several decades. He's known both for weighty academic works on Jesus and Paul, and for the more accessible \"For Everyone\" series aimed at general readers and small groups.\n\nHis For Everyone commentaries — including Matthew for Everyone, Mark for Everyone, Romans for Everyone, and Revelation for Everyone — walk through short passages with plain-language explanation and reflection questions, while his larger academic works on Paul and Jesus have reshaped much of contemporary scholarly conversation about first-century Judaism and early Christianity.",
