    name: 'Gordon Fee',
    tagline: 'NT scholar, Regent College',
    bio: "Gordon Fee (1934–2022) was an American New Testament scholar and ordained minister in the Assemblies of God who taught for many years at Regent College in Vancouver. He was widely respected across both Pentecostal and broader evangelical circles for his work on Pauline theology and New Testament textual criticism, as well as his popular guide to biblical interpretation, How to Read the Bible for All Its Worth, co-written with Douglas Stuart.\n\nHis commentaries — including The First Epistle to the Corinthians in the New International Commentary on the New Testament and Paul's Letter to the Philippians — are known for careful exegetical detail paired with attention to the Holy Spirit's work in the text, reflecting his Pentecostal theological background.",
